This function checks if all elements in query list `queries` exist in target list `corpus`:

```python
def check_all_present(corpus: list[int], queries: list[int]) -> bool:
    for q in queries:
        if q not in corpus:
            return False
    return True
```
Explain why this function runs in quadratic $O(M \times N)$ time, and rewrite it to execute in linear $O(M + N)$ time.

